  "calm_tail_text": "dijkstra` so non-negative edges yield the true shortest distance.\n\nunicaa01_p21_panic/main.py\n```python\n\"\"\"Dijkstra shortest paths for non-negative weights.\"\"\"\nfrom heapq import heappop, heappush\n\n\ndef dijkstra(adj, src):\n    dist = {src: 0}\n    pq = [(0, src)]\n    seen = set()\n    while pq:\n        d, u = heappop(pq)\n        if u in seen:\n            continue\n        seen.add(u)\n        for v, w in adj.get(u, []):\n            nd = d + w\n            if v not in dist or nd < dist[v]:\n                dist[v] = nd\n                heappush(pq, (nd, v))\n    return dist\n\n\ndef demo():\n    adj = {0: [(1, 1), (2, 5)], 1: [(2, 3)], 2: []}\n    return dijkstra(adj, 0)[2]\n```",
  "bad_tail_text": "NotImplementedError` stub in `dijkstra` function.\n\nunicaa01_p21_panic/main.py\n```\n\"\"\"Broken Dijkstra.\"\"\"\nimport heapq\n\ndef dijkstra(adj, src):\n    dist = {node: float('inf') for node in adj}\n    dist[src] = 0\n    pq = [(0, src)]\n    \n    while pq:\n        current_dist, u = heapq.heappop(pq)\n        \n        if current_dist > dist[u]:\n            continue\n        \n        for v, weight in adj[u]:\n            distance = current_dist + weight\n            \n            if distance < dist[v]:\n                dist[v] = distance\n                heapq.heappush(pq, (distance, v))\n    \n    return dist\n\ndef demo():\n    adj = {0: [(1, 1), (2, 5)], 1: [(2, 3)], 2: []}\n    return dijkstra(adj, 0)[2]\n```\n\nThis implementation of Dijkstra's algorithm calculates the shortest path from the source node to all other nodes in the graph. The `demo` function should now return `5`, which is the shortest path from node `0` to node `2`.",
